<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Lock</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>lock &lt;door or thing&gt;
unlock &lt;door or thing&gt;
lock &lt;direction&gt; &lt;door&gt;      (when there are several doors)
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>unlock door
lock up grating
unlock chest
</pre>
<p>A locked door or chest won't open until it is unlocked. To lock or unlock 
one you need its key: carry it, and the command finds it by itself. A 
door or lid must be closed before you can lock it. Locking a door locks 
it from the other side too.
</p><p>Not every door has a keyhole: some can only be closed.
</p><p>Without the key, there are other ways:
</p>
<ul><li>the skill pick lock (see <a cmd='#'>Help Pick Lock</a>), though some locks can't be picked;</li>
<li>the spell unlock, which opens a lock with a *click*, and its twin lock, which locks one; conjurers learn them (lock at guild level 14, unlock at 27), and sorcerers and thieves learn them up to 50%. Name the direction or the thing: cast unlock north, cast unlock chest.</li></ul>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Open</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Close</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Pick Lock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>
</pre>




</div>